1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,783
Reports can look finished after their inputs change.

2
00:00:03,783 --> 00:00:07,567
ProofFlow helps analytics agents keep saved work current.

3
00:00:07,567 --> 00:00:09,931
These briefs reuse earlier calculations.

4
00:00:09,931 --> 00:00:14,188
Every tool records the input versions it actually consumed.

5
00:00:14,188 --> 00:00:19,094
HydraDB connects those execution receipts across runs.

6
00:00:19,094 --> 00:00:25,050
Correct the euro-to-dollar rate from 1.10 to 1.20.

7
00:00:25,050 --> 00:00:27,177
The revenue claims become stale.

8
00:00:27,177 --> 00:00:32,507
ProofFlow withholds current values and labels the previous numbers as historical.

9
00:00:32,507 --> 00:00:33,726
Open the evidence.

10
00:00:33,726 --> 00:00:36,979
HydraDB shows the dependency path from

11
00:00:36,979 --> 00:00:40,881
that correction to this calculation and both reports.

12
00:00:40,881 --> 00:00:42,363
Refresh affected work.

13
00:00:42,363 --> 00:00:43,845
Four tools run.

14
00:00:43,845 --> 00:00:48,785
EU revenue becomes two thousand two hundred eighty dollars;

15
00:00:48,785 --> 00:00:52,737
company revenue becomes five thousand seven hundred fifty-five.

16
00:00:52,737 --> 00:00:56,351
The independent support result stays unchanged.

17
00:00:56,351 --> 00:01:03,720
Our frozen pilot has twelve authored scenarios, identical evidence, and a 2,048-token limit.

18
00:01:03,720 --> 00:01:07,688
ProofFlow refreshed 16 of 29 affected reports;

19
00:01:07,688 --> 00:01:14,490
BM25 refreshed six, dense retrieval one, and iterative hybrid nine.

20
00:01:14,490 --> 00:01:18,457
Every method shares the same Hydra-assisted executor.

21
00:01:18,457 --> 00:01:21,292
Exact dependency traversal ties ProofFlow.

22
00:01:21,292 --> 00:01:24,776
Full context completes all 29.

23
00:01:24,776 --> 00:01:30,202
Separately, two actual Fable 5.2 calls chose a seven-tool

24
00:01:30,202 --> 00:01:35,628
report workflow, then created a new brief reusing three earlier artifacts.

25
00:01:35,628 --> 00:01:38,095
All seventeen composition-and-refresh checks passed.

26
00:01:38,095 --> 00:01:44,664
This is recorded local model execution, separate from the guided browser demo.

27
00:01:44,664 --> 00:01:48,169
You can also import your own bounded CSV

28
00:01:48,169 --> 00:01:52,324
through the command line and reuse this same calculation runtime.

29
00:01:52,324 --> 00:01:56,071
ProofFlow: follow what changed, refresh what depends on

30
00:01:56,071 --> 00:02:00,000
it, and preserve work that remains valid.
